  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "On the ellipse, \\(|y|\\leq 1\\). The line \\(y=2\\) lies above the ellipse, so there are no intersection points.\n\nAlternative method 1: Substitute and exclude real solutions\n\nAn intersection point must satisfy both equations. Substituting \\(y=2\\) into the ellipse equation gives\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{4}+4=1,\n\\qquad x^2=-12.\n\\]\nA real square cannot be negative, so no real point satisfies both equations. The number of intersection points is \\(0\\).",
